@startuml Authentication Flow

' ============================================================================
' Authentication Flow Diagram
' ============================================================================
' This diagram shows how Bearer Token authentication works in the API.
' All endpoints (except /health) require a valid token in the Authorization header.
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2

title Bearer Token Authentication Flow

actor "API Client" as Client
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "HTTPBearer" as Bearer
participant "verify_token" as Auth
participant "Settings" as Config
participant "Router" as Router

== Successful Authentication ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer test-token-123
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Config : Get API_TOKENS
Config --> Auth : valid tokens list
Auth -> Auth : token in valid_tokens?
Auth --> Bearer : Valid
Bearer --> API : Authenticated
API -> Router : Process request
Router --> Client : 200 OK

== Invalid Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer wrong-token
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Config : Get API_TOKENS
Config --> Auth : valid tokens list
Auth -> Auth : token in valid_tokens?
Auth --> Client : 401 Unauthorized

== Missing Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nNo Authorization header
API -> Bearer : No token found
Bearer --> Client : 403 Forbidden

note right of Config
  Token Configuration:
  Env: API_TOKENS
  Format: JSON array
  Set in docker-compose.yml
end note

note right of Auth
  Security Features:
  Simple token comparison
  Stateless, no expiration
  Multiple tokens supported
end note

note left of Client
  Usage:
  curl with Authorization header
  Bearer token required
end note

@enduml
